1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A database field almost never belongs to one team.
Replace it, and a model, dashboard, or Spark job you do not own can fail.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
In one live test, repository analysis found one consumer.
Complete DataHub field lineage found thirty-one.
That is why DataHub changes the decision; it is not decoration.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Retirement Conductor turns that graph into one workflow:
discover, change, test natively, recheck,
then remove the old field—or refuse.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Codex is the operator. A project skill and sixteen-tool MCP server
let it inspect DataHub and drive the same campaign engine as the CLI.
It resolves the exact fields, finds one changeable dbt model,
and proposes one file change.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Then it stops. The agent cannot approve itself.
I review and authorize this exact digest outside the agent.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The approved change goes through a real pull request.
dbt parse, build, test, and semantic validation pass.
Retirement Conductor records the native receipt, rechecks DataHub,
writes the result back, and verifies that another agent can read it.

7
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The final command runs outside Codex with separate PostgreSQL credentials.
It freshly checks DataHub, the native consumers, approval, and producer schema.
In the clean run it commits exactly one drop, preserves the replacement,
the replacement Spark workload stays healthy, and replay is refused.

8
00:01:43,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Now the important case. After the original approval,
a Spark job appears in DataHub still reading legacy_status.
The same fresh reconciliation changes the answer to unsafe.

9
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Retirement Conductor performs zero destructive statements
and preserves the column. This is not a cosmetic warning:
in the matched static-signoff control, the drop goes through
and Spark fails with SQLSTATE 42703.

10
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:57,000
The Workbench reads that same campaign store: the exact cause,
consumers, change, validation, freshness, and event history.
It is deliberately not a privileged database console.
Retirement Conductor does not promise it found the universe.
It makes the evidence explicit, changes what it can prove,
and blocks the database change when that evidence changes.
